# Living Survey: Quantum_Computing                                                                                   
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Introduction                                                                                                      
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
This document collects the scientific literature regarding **Quantum_Computing**.                                    
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Emerging Architectures and Paradigms                                                                              
                                                                                                                     
Recent research explores alternatives to traditional transistor and qubit-based systems. [^10.34257_gjsfra257362]    
Proposes "atom computing," a paradigm where atoms replace transistors and controlled flows of single electrons or    
photons enable deterministic switching, addressing material scaling constraints in current quantum architectures.    
[^10.1109_mc.2021.3083430] Provides standardized engineering descriptions comparing digital, quantum, and biological 
computer architectures, contextualizing the performance potential and industry-standard models for quantum systems.  
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Quantum Algorithms and Optimization                                                                               
                                                                                                                     
Advancements in quantum algorithm design continue to address search space limitations. [^10.1007_s41066-022-00348-9] 
Introduces a hybrid granular computing approach to quantum genetic optimization, utilizing digital computers for     
fitness evaluation and quantum processors for population evolution to handle continuous optimization problems        
effectively. [^10.5120_ijca2021921834] Offers a comprehensive review of quantum computing fundamentals, detailing    
superposition and entanglement while exploring prospective applications across various industries and stakeholder    
domains.                                                                                                             
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Quantum Simulation and Software Tools                                                                             
                                                                                                                     
Open-source tools and simulation frameworks are expanding the accessibility of quantum research.                     
[^10.1016_j.cpc.2022.108598] Presents PULSEE, an open-source Python package for simulating magnetic resonance        
observables (NMR/NQR/ESR) using quantum gates and pulse sequences, bridging quantum information science with         
condensed matter research. [^10.1063_5.0151346] Provides a practical guide to applying quantum annealing to materials
science, demonstrating how to map defective graphene structures to qubits for configurational energy analysis.       
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Quantum Communication and Cryptography                                                                            
                                                                                                                     
Secure quantum communication protocols remain a critical research frontier. [^10.6084_m9.figshare.32051724] Details a
Python simulation of the BB84 Quantum Key Distribution (QKD) protocol, modeling state preparation, Born rule         
measurements, and classical post-processing to bridge theoretical concepts with practical implementation.            
[^https:__openalex.org_W7112574406] Explores quantum cryptography protocols (BB84, BB92, BB91) and Shor's algorithm  
implementation on quantum hardware, while analyzing vulnerabilities like photon splitting and faked-state attacks.   
[^10.31695_ijerat.2025.9.1] Introduces the Quantum Internet as a theoretical high-speed network for ultra-secure     
connectivity between quantum devices, outlining its transformative potential for global communications.              
[^10.5281_zenodo.6493704] Analyzes algorithmic improvements to dual lattice attacks against Learning With Errors     
(LWE), significantly reducing the security margins of NIST post-quantum cryptography finalists, highlighting the     
urgent need for quantum-resistant standards.                                                                         
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Applications in Engineering and Materials Science                                                                 
                                                                                                                     
Quantum computing is increasingly applied to complex engineering simulations. [^10.11159_icffts23.133] Reviews       
quantum computing applications in Computational Fluid Dynamics (CFD), discussing quantum algorithms for Navier-Stokes
equations and Lattice Boltzmann methods for aeronautical heat exchangers. [^10.21741_9781644902813-38] Presents a    
state-of-the-art review of quantum algorithms for CFD, specifically implementing a Lattice Boltzmann approach for 2D 
flow around a cylinder, demonstrating industrial applicability despite current implementation challenges.            
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Developer Ecosystem and Trends                                                                                    
                                                                                                                     
Understanding developer engagement is crucial for the maturation of quantum software ecosystems.                     
[^https:__openalex.org_W7155247427] Analyzes 1,404 Stack Overflow posts to map developer discussions on quantum      
toolchains, identifying hybrid quantum-classical computing and circuit implementation as dominant topics, with Qiskit
and Q-sharp leading community engagement. [^10.1007_978-3-031-90727-2_20] Demonstrates how open-source repositories  
(GitHub) and financial news can serve as pivotal indicators for tracking emerging quantum technology trends and      
market sentiment.                                                                                                    
                                                                                                                     

